  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "X[k] = sum over n of x[n] * exp(-2*pi*i*k*n/size)",
        "Bin k says how much of the signal turns at the frequency of that bin",
        "Worked out directly, that sum costs size*size steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "The radix-2 method of Cooley and Tukey splits the sum in half again and again",
        "That leaves log2(size) passes over the array, not size passes",
        "The two tables depend on the size alone, thus they are built at the allocation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it costs you",
      "items": [
        "The transform itself asks for no memory and works in the array you gave",
        "The tables hold size/2 turning factors and size indices",
        "A float holds about 7 digits; up to about 4096 points at least 4 survive"
      ]
    }
  ]
